From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(Hardware Support): KONKR Pocket FIT MCU buttons and Xbox port

Some Pocket FIT units expose no "AYANEO DEVICE" auxiliary keyboard in
either controller mode. Their Menu, Equals and K buttons and the LC/RC
pair arrive over the controller MCU's UART instead, through the same
konkr_sysbtn input device as the Pocket FIT Elite. Add it as a source
with the Elite's konkr3 map.

The Xbox mode pad was matched only on port 1 of the built-in USB
controller, but it enumerates on port 2 on these units. Match any port
on that controller.

---
--- a/rootfs/usr/share/inputplumber/devices/50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml
+++ b/rootfs/usr/share/inputplumber/devices/50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
     # XInput mode
     - group: gamepad
       evdev:
-          phys_path: usb-0001:01:00.0-1/input0
+          phys_path: usb-0001:01:00.0-*/input0
           vendor_id: 045e
           product_id: 028e
           handler: event*
@@ -44,6 +44,11 @@
           vendor_id: 1c4f
           product_id: 0002
           handler: event*
+    - group: keyboard
+      capability_map_id: konkr3
+      evdev:
+          name: KONKR System Buttons
+          handler: event*
 
 target_devices:
     - xbox-elite
